ass=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on Wilson County&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids January to February and February to March each came in under 90% of normal in 35 of 75 years. In 2026 so far, the middle of the grids sat at 56% of normal for February to March and 49% for March to April. Grids 19076 and 19376 had their driest year in 2007, at 66% of normal.</p>"}
